# Governed CVE waiver list for the InnBucks middleware image scan.
#
# RULES (a waiver without all three is a review failure):
#   * every entry carries: the CVE id, an owner, a one-line reason, and a
#     review-by date — as a comment directly above the id
#   * prefer fixing/upgrading over waiving; a waiver is a scheduled debt,
#     not a dismissal
#   * remove entries at their review date or renew them consciously
#
# The Release workflow scans CRITICAL/HIGH before it pushes, so a red gate
# blocks publication rather than reporting after the fact.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Alpine 3.23 — NO FIX AVAILABLE IN THE PINNED BRANCH.
#
# Trivy reports a "fixed version" for these, which is why --ignore-unfixed does
# not drop them, but that fix lands in a LATER Alpine branch. Verified against
# the base image:
#     apk policy libexpat p11-kit
#     libexpat: 2.8.1-r0 (only)     p11-kit: 0.25.5-r2 (only)
# There is nothing to upgrade to; the exit is a base-image bump when
# eclipse-temurin ships a 3.24-based 21-jre-alpine, which is also when these
# waivers should be deleted rather than renewed.
#
# owner: mpofuslim
# review by: 2026-10-31

# libexpat 2.8.1-r0 — handler call-depth tracking (56131) and copyString
# integer overflow (56408). Reached only via native XML parsing; this service
# parses JSON over HTTP and does not feed untrusted XML to expat, so the
# exposure is indirect at worst. Not a dismissal — revisit at the date above.
CVE-2026-56131
CVE-2026-56408

# p11-kit 0.25.5-r2 — NULL dereference via C_DeriveKey with specific NULL
# parameters. Requires a PKCS#11 token path; the middleware uses JKS/PKCS12
# files for TLS trust and no hardware/softoken PKCS#11 module.
CVE-2026-2100
